# GitHub formats (Russian, impersonal)
- Commit title `<тип>(<сервис>): <что сделано>`; squash adds ` (#NN)`.
- Types: `разработка`, `исправление`, `тесты`, `аналитика`, `инфраструктура`, `зависимости`, `документация`.
- Services: `чат`, `каталог`, `бронирование`, `identity`, `медиа`, `шлюз`, `фронт`, `ci`, `деплой`, `бд`, `общее`, `процесс`; wiki `вики`.
- Body (non-trivial):
  ```
  Зачем: <какую проблему решает>
  Как работает: <коротко, что поменялось>
  Задача: #NN
  ```
- Examples:
  ```
  исправление(медиа): подпись тела файла при загрузке в MinIO по HTTP (#60)

  Зачем: на dev POST /media/upload отвечал 500 на любой файл.
  Как работает: DisablePayloadSigning включается только для https, по http тело подписывается.
  Задача: #59
  ```
  ```
  разработка(каталог): публичная выдача туров (#61)
  ```
  ```
  инфраструктура(ci): проверка PR без деплоя, actions закреплены по SHA
  ```
  ```
  зависимости(фронт): обновить vitest и tinypool
  ```
- Dependabot `commit-message.prefix` per ecosystem (Dependabot appends the bump text after the prefix; no `include: scope`): nuget `зависимости(общее)`, npm `зависимости(фронт)`, docker `зависимости(деплой)`, github-actions `зависимости(ci)` (see `.github/dependabot.yml`).
- PR title = commit title without number. Sections: «Что сделано», «Зачем», «Как это работает» (simple example first), «Как проверить», «Документация» (имя страницы `Doc-` или «вики не затронута»), «Задача» (`#NN` only, or «без задачи» for rare docs/process-only meta PRs with no tracker task). Never «Учебный кейс» in PR/commits/issues (learning notes go only to the owner chat). Never use GitHub `closes`/`fix`/`fixes` in the PR body or commits before acceptance: merge must not auto-close the issue. Name the `Doc-` page to write after merge, or «вики не затронута». The wiki text itself is not part of the merge (`playbook-feature.mdc` «Doc-»). Impersonal Russian («убрано», not «убрал»): no personal names, no role labels as people, no agent or role as the actor, no «я/мы сделали», no `Co-authored-by` for bots. When clarity needs it, name Cursor Automations. Tick template checkboxes that hold.
- **Issue ↔ branch during work; closedBy only after close (unless Dependabot):** (1) branch `type/NN-short-english-slug` (ASCII lowercase English only; see `playbook-git-pr.mdc` «Branch naming»), created with `gh issue develop <NN> --name type/NN-short-english-slug --base main` so `linkedBranches` records the link (`gh issue develop --list <NN>`); (2) PR `## Задача` is `#NN` only, never `closes`/`fix`/`fixes`; (3) do not call `addCloseIssueReferences` and do not attach a closedBy / Development PR chip before acceptance. If the branch already exists, do not add or remove Development links by hand. The close workflow matches a merged PR when the issue number is its own branch segment and/or the PR title or body contains `#NN` (a closing keyword is not required). (4) Before merge, confirm that match is possible (linked branch or branch segment, plus `#NN` in «Задача»). Missing `#NN` on a tracked task is a process bug to fix in the PR text. Do not "fix" it with `addCloseIssueReferences`. Dependabot: no issue link. Docs-only meta with no tracker task: «без задачи». Do not retrofit old closed issues. (5) After Приёмка on dev, and after the named Doc- page is written when the PR named one: set `статус: готово`, then close the issue. A follow-up comment may note the merged PR. Workflow `.github/workflows/link-closed-by.yml` sets the Projects PR chip. Agents do not add or remove Development links after close. Carve-out for any manual Development add/remove: the owner explicitly asks.
- Comments (do not casually rewrite published ones; delete+repost only to remove a forbidden leak such as a personal name, a role label used as a person, a retired chat-bot name, or a secret). Short copy-paste: `.cursor/templates/issue-comment.md`. Full rule stays here:
  ```markdown
  **Итог:** одна фраза
  **Подробно:** факты, sha, шаги, без секретов
  **Дальше:** следующий шаг или «нет»
  ```
- Issue: title as commit; body «Зачем», «Что сделать», «Критерии приёмки» (testable), «Связи» (epic, the feature that spawned a bug-feature, issues, PR, wiki page). Epic children are features or bug-features (`playbook-workflow.mdc` «Types»). No third issue type. In issue/PR comments: no personal names, no role labels as people, no agent or role as the actor, no «я/мы сделали». When clarity needs it, name Cursor Automations. Otherwise write «взято в разработку», «ветка `…`», «PR #NN».
- Task types match that workflow: Epic (`тип: родительская`, field «Тип» = «Эпик», wiki `Epic-`) and Feature (issue + wiki `Feature-`). A bug-feature is a Feature with label `bug` and a link to the feature that spawned it. A typo inside an open feature is not a new issue. Do not add a label, a title prefix, or a wiki level for another analysis type. The `статус:*` label is the column. It does not add a type.
## Board statuses
The issue label is the stage and the Projects column. There is no second, coarser scale. Wiki pages do not carry a status line as source of truth.

- **Exactly one** of these labels on every open issue. Closed issues have only `статус: готово` (set it in the same moment as close). Agents set the label only. They do not move Projects cards, edit the Status field by hand, or edit view filters. `board-sync.yml` copies the label to the column. Carve-out: the owner explicitly asks to move a card.
- Create the matching GitHub label before the first use. The Project Status field needs one option per column name below (same spelling). Until an option exists, `board_order.py` leaves that card's column unchanged and the workflow exits with an error after the rest of the sync. Do not invent option ids in the script: it reads them by name.

| Label | Column | Who |
|---|---|---|
| `статус: очередь` | Очередь | both; nobody is on it |
| `статус: бизнес-анализ` | Бизнес-анализ | epic |
| `статус: аналитика` | Аналитика | feature, including bug-feature |
| `статус: архитектура` | Архитектура | both |
| `статус: разбиение` | Разбиение | epic |
| `статус: тест-кейсы` | Тест-кейсы | feature, including bug-feature |
| `статус: в работе` | В работе | epic only: child features in flight |
| `статус: разработка` | Разработка | feature, including bug-feature; includes PR review and the wait for Deploy |
| `статус: приёмка` | Приёмка | feature, including bug-feature; on dev after Deploy green |
| `статус: на ревью` | На ревью | owner decision. Epic: also owner epic acceptance after every child is Готово |
| `статус: готово` | Готово | closed after acceptance, or closed as not planned |
| `статус: удержание` | Удержание | paused; not part of the column sequence |

- On create → `статус: очередь` plus a type label (`bug` / `enhancement` / `documentation` / `question`, or `тип: родительская`). `тип: бэклог` is not a third route. The standing bugs epic is an ordinary epic.
- Advance to the next column only when the previous stage's artifacts are visible (`playbook-workflow.mdc`). No skipping on a product epic or feature.
- Epic sequence: Очередь → Бизнес-анализ → Архитектура → Разбиение → В работе → На ревью → Готово. Set В работе when the first child leaves Очередь. Keep it while any child is open. When every child is Готово, set На ревью (`playbook-epic.mdc`). The orchestrator owns that sync. `board-sync` does not infer the epic label from children.
- Feature sequence: Очередь → Аналитика → Архитектура → Тест-кейсы → Разработка → Приёмка → Готово. Code review is not На ревью: the feature stays Разработка until Deploy to dev is green, then Приёмка.
- Owner question: comment «**Итог:** требуется решение владельца» / «**Подробно:** вопрос, варианты, рекомендация» / «**Дальше:** после ответа вернуть колонку <название>», set `статус: на ревью`. Name the column to restore. After the answer, record «**Итог:** решено: ...» and restore that column. Do not restore a feature to В работе.
- Closing the GitHub issue moves the card to Готово (`board-sync`). Close only together with `статус: готово`, never from the PR body.
- Non-product issues (process docs, infra, questions) still use exactly one label. They are not a product feature: Очередь, Разработка, Приёмка when dev acceptance applies, Готово, and На ревью when the owner must decide. Dependabot has no issue.
- Views: «Задачи» (all except epics, by field «Тип») and «Эпики» («Тип» = «Эпик»). The Status field lists every column; empty columns on a view are expected. Ordinary tasks: no «Тип». Agents do not edit view filters.
- One-time relabel: an open feature that still has the old coarse `статус: в работе` is on the epic column. Set the feature's real column (usually `статус: разработка` or `статус: приёмка`). The script does not guess. An epic stays `статус: в работе` only while children are in flight.
- Card order: Очередь top = next; Готово newest closed first; other columns by issue number; Удержание is its own column. `board-sync.yml` (`.github/scripts/board_order.py`, on issue events, daily, manual) syncs columns, aligns status labels with open/closed, orders cards, adds missing issues, archives items closed 30+ days, clears «Приоритет» when a card leaves Очередь. How to choose numbers: **Queue priority** below.
- Labels: the orchestrator owns «Приоритет» and sets `статус:*` on take and finish. A cloud agent does not set labels. The architect brief calls out label drift; the orchestrator applies the label.
- **Process gaps (holistic):** any process inconsistency (labels, commits, PR wording, statuses, docs, branch links, closedBy chips, board, wiki, open PRs) is a symptom that order, staged delivery, or throughput may be drifting. Fix the live artifacts and update these rules / playbooks in the same delivery cycle. A process change must be deliberate and complete: before shipping it, scan related rules, templates, automations, board-sync, and recent examples for side effects; update every place that would otherwise diverge. Do not ship a local patch that breaks consistency elsewhere.
## Queue priority
Canonical method for field «Приоритет» on Очередь (1 = next). Finish the current product epic before the next roadmap epic. The owner may override any order with an explicit instruction.
### Layers
1. Roadmap (wiki `Plan-` / Plans) sets the coarse sequence of work.
2. Epic sequence or parallel sets follow the roadmap and wiki `Epic-` «Связи с другими эпиками».
3. Field «Приоритет» on Очередь cards ranks concrete tasks (1 = next).
### Epic selection
When the current product epic is Готово (or before the first take, if the owner has not chosen yet): propose the next epic or a parallel set from the roadmap and `Epic-` links (one epic when that is enough; a parallel set only when the owner confirms it). Then set «Приоритет» on those epics to match the agreed sequence and keep wiki and roadmap aligned. Detail: `playbook-epic.mdc` «Epic pick».
### Current epic first
Finish the current product epic, including bug-features spawned by its features, before moving to the next roadmap epic. The current epic is the one whose label is a stage other than Очередь, Готово, or Удержание. Unrelated discoveries go to the standing bugs epic (same feature columns, label `bug`) and do not stop this finish and do not jump ahead of it. Dependabot and non-product issues already in flight are not the next roadmap epic. The owner may still set an explicit order; that is an owner instruction, not a standing rule that the bugs epic outranks the current epic.
### Active epic to task priorities
For the current epic, raise its open Очередь children with contiguous low «Приоритет» numbers, ordered by dependency and delivery logic. If the owner has confirmed a parallel set, interleave those epics' children the same way, still ahead of the standing bugs epic and the rest of the backlog.
### Who sets «Приоритет»
Orchestrator only. `board-sync` / `board_order.py` never invents priority numbers: it sorts by the field, clears it when a card leaves Очередь, and orders Готово by newest closed.
### When to refresh
1. On demand when the owner asks (including a one-shot catch-up).
2. Weekly audit (orchestrator): verify Готово is newest-first; Очередь top is the current epic's children and the stated priorities; fix cheap mismatches. Do not invent a separate delete-branch ritual here.
3. On every new issue filed or accepted into the tracker: set «Приоритет» immediately so a current-epic child stays ahead of the standing bugs epic; adjust neighbors only as needed, not a full reshuffle every time.
### Fallback sort
After explicit «Приоритет»: other Очередь cards by issue number. `статус: удержание` is column Удержание, not the bottom of Очередь. A hold card that is still in Очередь (the column option is missing) sorts last (`board_order.py` `queue_key`). Unprioritized bugs do not outrank other unprioritized cards.
